                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "29995fa2-cf2b-4e0d-81a9-f0a5fc18bfd0",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "famished"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3339d875-66ce-3b04-af3f-ba876ebb2482",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To starve (to death); to kill or destroy with hunger."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9d4639f6-92d2-4648-a478-6b94b74d1cc0",
                                "sense_id": "3339d875-66ce-3b04-af3f-ba876ebb2482",
                                "text": "Even so did Corellius Rufus, another grave senator, by the relation of Plinius Secundus, Epist. lib.1, epist.12, famish himself to death […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "535dcd58-f497-30c6-9094-469cb673d81b",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To exhaust the strength or endurance of, by hunger; to cause to be very hungry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6bb4e1b-1c26-4343-a81f-64c64955bde3",
                                "sense_id": "535dcd58-f497-30c6-9094-469cb673d81b",
                                "text": "And when all the land of Egypt was famished, the people cried to Pharaoh for bread."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d122e5a1-6f2e-48cd-a43b-48ed7a5e7bc1",
                                "sense_id": "535dcd58-f497-30c6-9094-469cb673d81b",
                                "text": "The pains of famished Tantalus [he] shall feel."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5f3c28e0-dbb9-3362-aefc-81d84350b1b8",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To kill, or to cause great suffering to, by depriving or denying anything necessary."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e4dbf5a-b168-4402-885a-4b734bc8b05e",
                                "sense_id": "5f3c28e0-dbb9-3362-aefc-81d84350b1b8",
                                "text": "And famish him of breath, if not of bread?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4be15cae-c6ee-3563-bc1a-57244a4de450",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To force, control, or constrain by famine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9d9bd3a-c741-461a-896e-2f4b205155f5",
                                "sense_id": "4be15cae-c6ee-3563-bc1a-57244a4de450",
                                "text": "He had […]famished Paris into a surrender."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c5cfd821-facd-3198-8c59-3ba4b613efae",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To die of hunger; to starve to death."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fff05bbe-9917-4fa2-a7bd-0718dfc5d285",
                                "sense_id": "c5cfd821-facd-3198-8c59-3ba4b613efae",
                                "text": "Some ſay that Rauens foſter forlorne children, / The vvhilſt their ovvne birds famiſh in their neſts: / Oh be to me though thy hard hart ſay no, / Nothing ſo kinde but ſomething pittifull."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7111c736-aa43-33df-bf6c-55f8c17f8599",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To suffer extreme hunger or thirst, so as to be exhausted in strength, or to nearly perish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7d15627-6538-4e4c-b979-00255166e243",
                                "sense_id": "7111c736-aa43-33df-bf6c-55f8c17f8599",
                                "text": "You are all resolved rather to die than to famish?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "73367401-451f-35a1-9a8e-cd3e2b16dd83",
                        "entry_id": "0722ed86-b976-3891-927f-8db000dff332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To suffer extremity from deprivation of anything essential or necessary."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5aa1d03-5c18-449b-9793-df6beb285ba5",
                                "sense_id": "73367401-451f-35a1-9a8e-cd3e2b16dd83",
                                "text": "The Lord will not suffer the soul of the righteous to famish."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
